+# Feature Specification: Cancel Booking
+
+**Created**: 2026-10-21 | **Status**: Draft
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Cancel a booking (P1)
+A customer asks to cancel; `cancel(bookingId, at)` cancels at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Cancelling before the rental starts refunds the full total.
+2. Cancelling once the rental has started (but not ended) refunds 0.
+3. After cancelling, the item is free again for the period (`book`, `availability`).
+4. A second cancel of the same booking is rejected.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- Unknown booking id, invalid `at`, or `at` at/after the booking's end: rejected.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `cancel` validates `at` as an ISO-8601 UTC instant.
+- **FR-002**: Refund = total if `at` < start, else 0.
+- **FR-003**: A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment; it can be cancelled only once.
+
+## Assumptions
+- The refund policy was not specified in the request; full-before-start / none-after-start is the simplest
+  assumption and needs confirmation by the business.
